  "content": {
    "id": "p66-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Consider the equation $3x^{2}+kx+1=0$.\nFind values of $k$ for which the equation has one, two, or no solutions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p66-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "One solution $\\Delta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=\\pm2\\sqrt{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=k^{2}-4(3)(1)\\\\&=k^{2}-12\\end{align*}$$\nFor one real solution, $\\Delta=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}k^{2}-12&=0\\\\k^{2}&=12\\\\k&=\\pm2\\sqrt{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p66-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Two solutions $\\Delta>0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k<-2\\sqrt{3}$ or $k>2\\sqrt{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=k^{2}-4(3)(1)\\\\&=k^{2}-12\\end{align*}$$\nFor two real solutions, $\\Delta>0$.\n$$k^{2}-12>0$$\nThe parabola $y=k^{2}-12$ opens upwards and crosses the horizontal axis at $k=\\pm2\\sqrt{3}$. It is above the axis outside these intercepts.\n$$k<-2\\sqrt{3}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad k>2\\sqrt{3}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p66-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "No solutions $\\Delta<0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2\\sqrt{3}<k<2\\sqrt{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=k^{2}-4(3)(1)\\\\&=k^{2}-12\\end{align*}$$\nFor no real solutions, $\\Delta<0$.\n$$k^{2}-12<0$$\nThe parabola $y=k^{2}-12$ opens upwards and crosses the horizontal axis at $k=\\pm2\\sqrt{3}$. It is below the axis between these intercepts.\n$$-2\\sqrt{3}<k<2\\sqrt{3}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      }
    ]
  },
